{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review the quality and oversight of Child DLA decision-making",
        "additional_details": "We call for such a review to consider:\r\n\u2022 Whether child DLA decisions accurately reflect the evidence and give clear reasons to claimants.\r\n\u2022 Where decisions change at MR or tribunal, examine why and whether issues could have been resolved earlier.\r\n\u2022 Recurring problems and inform improvements using root-cause analysis.\r\n\u2022 Whether changes improve first-time decision quality and reduce avoidable disputes and stress for families.\r\n\u2022 Lessons from changed decisions should feed back into future decision-making.",
        "background": "Review the Child Disability Living Allowance (DLA) decision process, including how decisions are assessed and ensure they are regularly independently overseen. A review should include considering initial decisions, Mandatory Reconsiderations (MR) and tribunal outcomes.",
